#: freeports_dev.ci:1 of
msgid ""
"The measurements, the thresholds and the gate -- what a commit to this "
"repository must clear."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci:3 of
msgid "Three layers, and nothing in one layer knows the next:"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci:5 of
msgid ""
"**measurement** -- each command answers one question and writes one small"
" normalised JSON file into ``reports/``. None of them decides anything;"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci:7 of
msgid ""
"**the gate** -- :mod:`freeports_dev.ci.gate` reads those files, "
"``ci.yaml`` and the class of the current branch, prints one table and "
"chooses an exit status;"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci:9 of
msgid ""
"**the wiring** -- ``make`` targets in the engine repository and a thin "
"hook in each of the others."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci:11 of
msgid ""
"It is the split ``freeports-validate`` already follows -- ``collect`` "
"establishes facts, ``report`` renders them, ``check-grants`` judges them "
"-- and it is what keeps every figure reproducible by hand, which is the "
"only way a threshold survives its first failure."
msgstr ""

